        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(android): show Canvas outside Settings",
        "body": "Related: #101859\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Android users invoking `canvas.present`, `canvas.navigate`, or A2UI commands while outside the Settings Screen view would receive a successful command result without a usable visible Canvas surface.\n\nThis addresses the Canvas portion of #101859. It does not change camera or location command exposure, permissions, or gateway authorization policy.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nCanvas presentation is now owned by the app shell through one retained WebView host with explicit unmounted, hidden, and visible states. Commands are serialized through that host, A2UI content requests presentation, Settings controls the same host instead of embedding a second one, and renderer recovery replaces a crashed WebView without replaying the crashing URL.\n\nThe shell also owns safe drawing bounds and Canvas background coverage, so content respects system insets without exposing the underlying app at the edges.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAndroid Canvas and A2UI content can now appear from Home and other app surfaces, hide cleanly through Back or close actions, survive rotation, and recover after renderer loss. Hidden Canvas state no longer blocks interaction with the underlying app.\n\nCanvas commands complete when the host accepts the operation rather than waiting for remote page loading, while background presentation requests continue to fail explicitly instead of creating a deferred overlay.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Live Android 15 E2E: reproduced the detached Canvas behavior on the prior path, then verified shell presentation from Home, Settings entry and exit, system Back, close and hide, A2UI JSON and JSONL push/reset, external HTTPS navigation, snapshot capture, slow-page command completion, failed-page recovery, repeated present/hide cycles, and portrait/landscape rotation.\n- Live renderer-loss proof: forced a Chromium renderer crash, observed one crash callback, verified a replacement scaffold, and confirmed the prior crashing URL was not replayed.\n- Live inset/input proof: verified Canvas content below the status bar with covered gutters, then hid Canvas and navigated Settings through the underlying shell.\n- Live lifecycle proof: verified a foreground-to-background race returns `NODE_BACKGROUND_UNAVAILABLE` and does not present later.\n- Android instrumentation: `CanvasHostLifecycleTest` passed all 4 lifecycle and renderer scenarios.\n- Android build: `node scripts/run-android-gradle.mjs :app:clean :app:assemblePlayDebug :app:assemblePlayDebugAndroidTest`.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kx50d3119m1acwsr391k7fj1`: `corepack pnpm android:test` and `corepack pnpm check:changed`.\n- Fresh pre-commit autoreview completed with no accepted or actionable findings.\n\nAI-assisted: yes.\n",
